Your natural form is actually usually a good choice for the endgame.
If you're bent on being something else, try a master mind flayer (if you
haven't genocided them).  They can wear all armor, have a natural AC of 0,
fly, and do plenty damage against brainful critters*.  Just watch out for 
footrices, just as you do with a dragon, vampire (lord), or anything else
with an innate bare-body attack.  They make nice pets, too.

*Vampire lords have most of the same advantages, except a generally
less potent innate attack (level drain instead of brain eating).
I find that brainful critters immune to level-drain are more of a 
problem that brainless creatures susceptable to level-drain (demons,
angels, and that lot).


